From 6583f10e12899cc58103ad3cf13431edb19010a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manas Kamal Choudhury <manaskamal.kandupur@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:24:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(KernelAA64): bring up secondary cores through PSCI
 CPU_ON

First SMP milestone for KernelAA64. Every core under /cpus with
enable-method = "psci" is started, switches to the boot core's
translation regime, reaches higher half C, prints
"From SMP : <n>" over UART and parks in wfi with irqs masked.

- Hal/aa64smpboot.s: PSCI hvc/smc conduits and a position
  independent trampoline. Drops EL2 -> EL1 when ATF hands the core
  over in EL2 (iMX8MP), sets FPU/NEON, VBAR, MAIR, TCR, TTBR0/1,
  turns the MMU on and branches to AA64SMPAPEntry.
- Hal/aa64smp.c: walks /cpus, picks the PSCI conduit from
  /psci method, copies the trampoline into a fresh boot page and
  hands each core an AA64SMPBootParam (context_id) plus a 16K stack.
  Cores are started one at a time; the boot core polls CNTPCT for
  up to 500ms for each to report in.
- The AP runs its last trampoline instructions with the MMU on, so
  the boot page gets a private 1GB identity map in TTBR0 instead of
  the firmware one (edk2 maps free RAM execute-never, and the low
  half is torn down by AuVmmngrBootFree). AA64SMPAPEntry restores
  the boot core's TTBR0/TCR first thing.
- dtb.c: AuDeviceTreeGetChildNode and AuDeviceTreeGetStringProperty,
  the existing prefix lookup can't enumerate /cpus.
- init.c: AA64SMPInitialize() after board init.
- build_and_run_qemu.sh: -smp, XENEVA_QEMU_SMP (default 4).

Not yet: GIC CPU interface/timer per core, scheduler, spin-table
(RPi3). Spinlocks from AuCreateSpinlock(false) are still no-ops.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
